+// The voice-message strip is absolutely positioned in the band right under
+// the navbar (see GlobalVoiceMessagePlayer/styles.module.scss). Reserve
+// exactly its 38px there — as a navbar margin, so the navbars stay put and
+// the scrolling areas below them start 38px lower — instead of letting it
+// overlay and click-block the top of the chat list / message list.
+//
+// ponytail: the mechanism is the sibling combinator alone — the strip is
+// MainScreen's first child and only mounts when it is the active surface, so
+// no JS, no class to keep in sync, and no strip in the DOM (wide screen,
+// setting off, nothing playing) means byte-identical layout. It does hard-wire
